gamewindow-vtable-lead-refuted	0x0078FDE0	1	identified	LEAD REFUTED, and the premise was mine. drawCheckBoxText at 0x0078FDE0 was framed as evidence that BFME's GameWindow vtable carries extra virtual slots, on the strength of an extra call through [edx+0x38] and several shifted slot offsets. That framing does not survive inspection: EVERY diverging vtable call in this function dispatches through the DisplayString object, loaded from WinInstanceData::m_text at +0x19C - not through GameWindow at all. The calls that do go through the window pointer (winGetScreenPosition, winGetSize, winGetStatus, winGetFont and the colour getters) are non-virtual per GameWindow.h, compile to direct calls in both retail and ours, and never diverge. So there is no GameWindow vtable evidence here in either direction. Worse for generalising, this single call site's own deltas are internally INCONSISTENT, which is the same signature that killed the earlier DX8 IDirect3DDevice8 investigation (7 slots at some sites, 1 at another) and means no single insertion-point model fits. reverse/vtables.tsv has no DisplayString or GameWindow rows to seed a slot table from either. Do not reopen this on the GameWindow framing. A DisplayString-specific investigation seeded from matched callers that make exactly one virtual call might still be viable, but nothing here supports it yet
