adjacency-cluster-multiplier	0x00912010	22	converted	BEST RUN SO FAR - 22 rows in one session against a previously measured baseline of a couple per session, all through the adjacency lane and tools/find_gaps.py. The multiplier is identified and reusable: WORK FILE CLUSTERS, NOT ONE-OFF GAPS. Once one trivial getter in a class is verified, its siblings share the same offset arithmetic, the same header declaration order and the same mangling pattern, so each additional row costs almost nothing. pointgr.cpp went 5 of 5 and linegrp.cpp 4 of 4 on exactly that basis (PointGroupClass and LineGroupClass trivial-getter clusters). SECOND MULTIPLIER: C source files have no name mangling at all, so the identification step that dominates cost in C++ simply vanishes - sb_server.c yielded 3 and sb_serverbrowsing.c 2 clean hits by reading field offsets straight out of struct definitions in sb_internal.h. Measured hit rates, which differ sharply by how the pool is filtered: on gaps whose two flanking matched rows come from the SAME source file, 7 of 23 landed (30 percent); on the raw unfiltered high-half list, 15 of 516 (about 3 percent) though effort was concentrated on roughly 8 files after triage. So the same-source-file flank test is worth roughly a tenfold improvement in candidate quality and should always be applied first. Pool remaining: 9 unexplored template-ctor gaps in fx_particle_system_bulk.cpp, and about 211 low-half gaps whose flanking files DIFFER - a weaker signal but not worthless. ActiveBody's neighbourhood is now exhausted; its remaining 36 unclaimed definitions are scattered non-adjacently and are not reachable by this lane
home-tu-not-adjacency-tu	0x00087400	2	tooling	IMPORTANT CORRECTION to the adjacency method, caught twice in one session. The file the adjacency heuristic points at - the source of the two flanking matched rows - is NOT necessarily the file that must be passed to add_match. A function declared inline in a vendored header is emitted as a COMDAT only in the translation unit that actually ODR-USES it, which can be a completely different file. getEventName@AudioEventRTS lives at 0x00087400 but had to be claimed against GameAudio.cpp rather than AudioEventRTS.cpp, and getFirstView@Display at 0x0040F5D0 against W3DDisplay.cpp rather than Display.cpp. The good news is that this fails SAFELY and diagnostically: add_match's own compile-and-verify step reports 'symbol not found in object' and auto-reverts with no side effects, so the cost is one cheap retry against the file that actually calls the function. When a candidate looks right but the symbol will not emit, ask WHICH TU CALLS IT rather than assuming the placement was wrong. Related failure worth recording separately: isUnderConstruction@AIPlayer looked like a clean getter but is never called anywhere in the Code tree, so no TU emits it at all and it cannot be landed from any file
icf-first-claimant-recurs		5	identified	The ICF trap recurred repeatedly in this sweep and is now the dominant failure mode in the adjacency lane, so it deserves restating as a working rule rather than a footnote. Byte-identical trivial accessors get folded by the linker and the FIRST CLAIMANT OWNS THE ADDRESS, which means a plausible-looking gap candidate is frequently a name already matched elsewhere against an unrelated function. Concrete instances abandoned this run: two fld [ecx+N] / ret candidates near part_emt.cpp and v3_rnd.cpp resolved to names already matched elsewhere through ICF folds to unrelated functions; empty no-op virtual overrides in ControlBar.cpp and InGameUI.cpp (createMoveHint) are shared byte-for-byte by three or more sibling classes in the same file, and already-claimed siblings proved the ambiguity was real; a mov eax,ecx / ret identity thunk and a vtable-init ctor candidate were abandoned for lack of corroborating call sites. The rule: for any body under about 8 bytes, ambiguity is the DEFAULT and corroboration is mandatory before landing. The cheap corroboration that worked all session is a gen-thunk row elsewhere in functions.csv whose target= field points exactly at the gap's start RVA. Every one of the 22 rows landed this run had that witness. Two candidates that lacked it were abandoned even though they looked correct
gen-alias-object-symbol-claimable	0x002C7D70	7	converted	A claimable-row pattern worth knowing, found while landing getBuildSubTask@WorkerAIUpdate at 0x002C7D70 (7 bytes). Its mangled name did not appear as a pinned name anywhere; it existed ONLY as the object-symbol target of two already-matched gen-alias dup_ rows elsewhere in the same file. That is not an ODR conflict and does not make the address unavailable - the dup_ rows alias the name, but the true instance at its own address was unclaimed and could be claimed directly under the real name. So when a name appears solely as an object-symbol or dup-of target in existing rows, check whether the genuine instance is still free rather than assuming the name is taken. One pin was also added this run for a different reason worth noting: _SBLastListErrorA at 0x008680B0, the jmp target of the tail-call forwarder _ServerBrowserListQueryErrorA. add_match's own byte-verifier caught the unresolved call and named the exact symbol required, which is the cheapest possible way to discover a needed pin - let the verifier tell you
witness-rule-was-too-strict		17	tooling	RULE CORRECTION, and the error was mine. After the 22-row run I wrote the gen-thunk witness test - find a row in functions.csv whose target= field points exactly at the gap's start RVA - into the method as MANDATORY before landing any adjacency candidate. That is wrong as an absolute. A thunk only exists for functions reached through a vtable slot or an ILT stub; a PLAIN NON-VIRTUAL MEMBER CALL has no thunk anywhere, so no witness can possibly exist for it. Making the witness mandatory therefore excludes an entire legitimate class of candidate by construction. It cost real yield this run: the C-source lane found 12 plausible bodies (struct-field getters and setters, zero-init helpers, call wrappers, a byte-swap helper), found no witness for any of them because none are virtual, and correctly-per-my-rules landed nothing. Meanwhile the Libraries lane landed Get_Buffer_Size and Get_Initial_Orientation_Random at 0x0097E0B0 and 0x0097E0C0 with NO witness at all, because they are plain member getters, by relying on add_match's own compile-and-BYTE-VERIFY step - which is the actual arbiter and cannot be fooled. CORRECTED RULE: the witness is strong corroboration WHERE ONE CAN EXIST, and is worth searching for first. Where the function is non-virtual and no thunk exists, a byte-verified compile through add_match is sufficient on its own. The witness remains genuinely REQUIRED only for the ICF-ambiguous shapes - bare ret, ret 4, mov eax,1, xor eax,eax, mov eax,ecx identity thunks - where many distinct functions share identical bytes and the compile cannot distinguish them
