two-mechanisms-make-the-result-generalise		59602	identified	WHY THE ZERO IS NOT A SAMPLING ACCIDENT - two mechanisms in the existing toolchain do the work, and both are structural rather than incidental. FIRST, build.py's build_call_thunks() DISCOVERS INCREMENTAL-LINK THUNKS FROM THE IMAGE ITSELF and adds them as candidate addresses for any matched name, so the whole 'callee is reached through an ILT thunk' case - which is 14 of the 21 distinct targets in the sample - resolves with no human action at all. That is also why a target can look unpinned while being perfectly resolvable, and it is the same fact that dissolved two supposed blockers earlier in the session. SECOND, symbols.csv IS ADDITIVE AND ALREADY HOLDS 59602 ?b_ BODY PINS, so a name can acquire another candidate address without disturbing any existing claim. TOGETHER THEY MEAN THE DEPENDENCY GRAPH IS MOSTLY ALREADY SATISFIED, which is precisely what my address-coverage measurements could not see: they asked whether the ledger covers an address, when the question was whether a NAME the source can spell has that address among its candidates
