a-ledger-name-refuted-by-the-bytes-it-names	0x003BDB80	1	identified	A DEFECT IN THE EXISTING LEDGER, FOUND BY READING RATHER THAN BY A CHECK, AND LEFT UNTOUCHED BECAUSE FIXING IT IS ITS OWN JOB. 0x003BDB80 is matched as ?addSnapshotBlock@GameState@@AAEXVAsciiString@@PAVSnapshot@@W4SnapshotType@@@Z, and that row came from an __emit lift - WHICH BYTE-MATCHES BY CONSTRUCTION AND THEREFORE PROVES NOTHING ABOUT THE SIGNATURE. THE BYTES REFUTE THE NAME: the body ends in a BARE ret, and its caller at 0x003BFA60 reaches it with `mov ecx,esi / call` AND NO PUSHES AT ALL. A function declared to take an AsciiString by value plus two more arguments cannot end in a bare ret and cannot be called with an empty stack. The lane did not pin a contradicting name and did not land 0x003BFA60, which stays unclaimed rather than resting on a signature the bytes deny. WORTH GENERALISING: AN __emit-LIFTED ROW IS A BYTE RECORDING, NOT AN IDENTIFICATION, so any signature attached to one is an assertion nobody has checked - and the cheapest check is the caller's stack.
span-tightness-predicts-coherence-but-not-perfectly	0x003B8450	41	converted	CALIBRATION ON MY OWN FILE-SELECTION HEURISTIC, WHICH IS WORTH RECORDING BECAUSE THE NEXT RUN DEPENDS ON IT. I chose this run's four files by SPAN TIGHTNESS rather than row count, reasoning that rows packed into 27-41 KB are far likelier to be one translation unit than rows smeared over 1.9 MB. THREE OF FOUR CAME BACK COHERENT - Object.cpp, the FESL SDK, and the FXParticleSystem module-info hierarchy. THE FOURTH DID NOT: d_003b8450.asm is a MIXED region, roughly a third STLport container machinery, a third small ICF-folded leaf code that lands there from all over the image, and only a third a genuine subsystem - and it was that last third, identifiable because its bodies call each other through ILT thunks that land back INSIDE the same span, that produced all 41 rows. SO SPAN TIGHTNESS IS A GOOD PRIOR AND NOT A GUARANTEE, and the confirming test is INTERNAL CALL LOCALITY: a real TU's bodies call each other. A region whose callees all point outward is a linker-ordering artefact, not a source file. THAT TEST IS CHEAP AND SHOULD BE PART OF SELECTION NEXT TIME, not discovered per-lane.
