vendored-2004-headers-beat-reconstructed-2007-ones	0x008654A0	106	identified	THE LOAD-BEARING FIND OF THE RUN, AND IT IS A LAYOUT FACT RATHER THAN A SHAPE ONE. Six GameSpy Chat/Peer translation units lie end to end in 0x00860020..0x00866400 - chatMain.c, peerPing.c, peerPlayers.c, peerRooms.c, peerKeys.c, peerHost.c - all reconstructed from the 2007 SDK because the 2004 carrier ships no chat/ or peer/ module. EVERY peerKeys.c BODY MISSED BY A CONSTANT OFFSET UNTIL THE HEADERS WERE MIXED: the 2007 peerMain.h makes SBServerList and SBQueryEngine POINTER TYPEDEFS, while the VENDORED 2004 serverbrowsing/sb_internal.h makes them STRUCTS BY VALUE. That is 3028 bytes inside piConnection and it moves the watch-key block from +0x0CD8 to +0x18C4. With the 2004 definitions every body went byte-exact. Likewise 2004's chatGlobalCallbacks has FIVE members where 2007 has eight, putting loginType at +0x08A8. THE GENERAL RULE: WHEN RECONSTRUCTING FROM A LATER SDK, TAKE EVERY STRUCT THAT THE VENDORED CONTEMPORARY TREE ACTUALLY DEFINES FROM THE VENDORED TREE - the later text is a guide to CODE, not to LAYOUT. Two further places where retail plainly carries the OLDER text were followed against 2007 rather than with it: ciNickIsValid uses the pre-2004 isdigit/'-' rule that 2007 comments out, and chatConnectDoit passes its serverAddress/port PARAMETERS to ciSocketConnect.
