?bfmeShrinkVNT@BfmeVecVNT@@,0x0087FB90,77,residue,"Copies through the helper 0x0087EA20 - passing the second argument, the current end, the first argument, the address of the first argument's own home slot and a zero - then releases the string at +0x1c of every element from the returned end up to the old end, stores the new end and returns the first argument. Size exact at 77 with the whole call, the five-argument cleanup, the 0x24 stride, the free alignment nop and the loop all matching. Retail reads the first argument into edx before the four callee-saved pushes and keeps this in edi with the result in ebx; MSVC reads it after the pushes and keeps this in ebx with the result in ebp. Reordering the three loop locals does not move it, and reading the argument into a local at the top costs four bytes. Third instance of the same argument-load-position difference, after 0x009D1C50 and 0x0086F7C0: retail hoists a parameter read above the prologue pushes where MSVC leaves it below."
