?bfmeFillVOD@BfmeOwnerVOD@@,0x006A3130,167,residue,"Tops the list at +0x9c0 up to the configured limit: counts the list, and while short of the limit makes an item through the factory pointer, initialises it, counts again to pass the new one-based index to the setter, allocates a 0xc node, stores the item through the guarded member address, links the node before the sentinel and bumps the count; on either exit it copies the config field at +0x30 into +0x618. Size exact at 167 with both inline count loops, both alignment nops free, the three __stdcall pointer calls with no cleanup, the cdecl allocator's own cleanup, and the placement-style null check on the node member. Two things were needed: hoisting the setter pointer into a local so it lives in ebp across the outer loop, and making both exits break so the tail assignment is shared rather than duplicated. What remains is the ebx and edi pair: retail keeps the item in edi and the sentinel copy in ebx, MSVC the reverse. Declaring the sentinel local before the item, and hoisting the item's declaration outside the loop, both leave it unchanged."
