?bfmeCopyBackVPD@@,0x008954A0,101,residue,"Refcounted backward assign over pointer slots: for each position other than where source and destination coincide, releases the destination's referent - decrementing, and on reaching zero running its destructor and freeing eighteen hex bytes through the global deleter - then stores the source pointer and add-refs it. 113 bytes on the first shape. Retail reads the destination argument first, before any push, and derives the destination end with one lea; it also performs three separate null-and-count tests on the destination slot, re-reading it from memory between them, where an and-chain plus one re-read generates more. Next shape to try: three nested flat ifs, each re-reading through the destination pointer rather than a cached local. Two neighbours from this same screen, 0x002EA550 and 0x002EB010, were converted exactly but lost to a claim race during landing."
