?bfmeCopyVTL@@YAPAUBfmeElemVTL@@PAU1@00@Z,0x003AEBB0,117,residue,"__cdecl(first, last, dest) copy loop over 0x20-byte elements, returning dest unchanged: per element three UnicodeString::set(const &) calls at +0x00, +0x10 and +0x14 (0x00887C90) plus scalar copies at +4, +8, +0xc (byte) and +0x18, with the induction pointers biased +4 so the first string is [esi-4]. Element layout and body order are certain from the displacements. The gap is the prologue: retail computes (last - first) >> 5 using only eax and ecx, branches, and only then pushes ebx/ebp/esi/edi and RELOADS first, last and dest inside the guard, so the empty path returns dest straight from the stack in five bytes. Every source form keeps first in a callee-saved register across the guard (edi at 109 bytes, ebx at 111) because it is live into the loop, and MSVC common-subexpressions the reload away. Taking local copies of all three parameters inside the guard does not break the CSE. The twin at 0x003B33C0 (117) is the same body, and 0x003AEC50/0x003B3460 (86) are the smaller two-field version already logged with a related preheader residue."
