?bfmeCopyVTL@@YAPAUBfmeElemVTL@@PAU1@00@Z,0x003AEBB0,117,residue,"Follow-up: volatile does not break the parameter CSE here. Marking the parameters volatile changes the mangled name (MSVC encodes top-level cv on parameters, so the symbol is not found), and re-reading them through a volatile cast -- src = *(T *volatile *)&first -- forces the load but MSVC still keeps a callee-saved register live across the guard (110 bytes with first only, 105 with first and dest) and additionally flips the subtraction operand order because the volatile read cannot be reordered. Retail computes (last - first) >> 5 in eax and ecx alone with no push before the jle. Still open."
